ritical need for precise dosing and regular monitoring to avoid life-threatening hemorrhagic events. [Data: Relationships (9471, 9508)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"葡萄糖酸钙 is contraindicated with地高辛 due to potential cardiac toxicity\",\n            \"explanation\": \"葡萄糖酸钙 is contraindicated for use with 地高辛 because concurrent administration can increase the risk of cardiac arrhythmias and digitalis toxicity. Calcium enhances the effects of digoxin on cardiac myocytes, potentially leading to dangerous electrophysiological disturbances. While the provided evidence focuses more broadly on infusion compatibility issues, the established clinical guideline remains clear: calcium salts should be used with extreme caution—if at all—in patients receiving digoxin. [Data: Relationships (7261)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"高岭土 significantly reduces地高辛 absorption\",\n            \"explanation\": \"高岭土, an adsorbent antidiarrheal agent, markedly decreases the absorption of 地高辛 when co-administered. Evidence shows that co-ingestion of kaolin-pectin with digoxin can reduce its absorption by up to 62%. This occurs through physical adsorption of digoxin onto the surface of kaolin particles, preventing its dissolution and uptake in the gastrointestinal tract. To mitigate this interaction, clinicians should separate the administration times of these agents by at least 2 hours or consider alternative formulations. [Data: Relationships (34318)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"含鞣质较多的中草药 impair absorption of利福平 and other antibiotics\",\n            \"explanation\": \"中草药 rich in tannins—including rhubarb, gallnut, and agrimony—can form insoluble tannate complexes when co-administered with basic antibiotics like 利福平 (rifampin). These precipitates reduce the bioavailability of both the herbal and pharmaceutical agents. This interaction exemplifies a broader class of physicochemical drug-herb incompatibilities that compromis